// @no-instantiate
// @hint redundant type annotation: `useShape` is inferred as `i32`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `sqv` is inferred as `{s: i32}`
// @hint Intentionally-unused variable `_sp1`
// @hint Intentionally-unused variable `_sp2`
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: a nullable union-box field read through a map-of-map hop, with NO twin
// declaration anywhere in the file. `vl check` exits 0 (four HINTs, no errors) and is the ONLY
// command that misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl check --codegen --no-validate`
// exits 0, `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed.)
//
// THE MECHANISM. `Box1` and `Box2` are container ALIASES of the same map layout — D88's
// claimant count — and the sentence is ONE sentence across the whole family: two different
// heap types behind one placeholder, which is D39/D100's seam rather than a field-read
// message. Put `type Dot = { r: i32 | null }` / `type DotB = { db: i32 }` /
// `type DotU = Dot | DotB` back and the compiler turns LOUD instead
// (`emitProgram: bare null needs a struct-typed context`) — the declaration the program never
// mentions again is the only thing diagnosing it, which is D224's whole finding and the reason
// this twin-FREE spelling is the honest population.
//
// WHY THIS ONE — AND THE PROPERTY IS A CENSUS, NOT AN ARGUMENT. The slot's last three
// selection rules each failed within a day of being written, so the successor is again picked
// by RUNNING every row of `silent-class-inventory.md` against this tree rather than by
// reasoning about which family a program belongs to. All 138 rows' own filed programs were
// graded (`python3 scripts/check-filed-witnesses.py --strict`); exactly TWO are check-clean
// invalid wasm — D291, which the commit that pinned this file CLOSES, and D300, which is this
// one. **After D291 closes, this is the only live member of the class.**
//
// AND THE CAVEAT IS STATED RATHER THAN GLOSSED. This program is NOT out of reach: it is
// D224's remaining price, and D224's own cut takes exactly these 27 census-block-B coordinates
// from a loud emit reject to here. The row that owns it (D300) says closing them takes D224's
// price to zero, so the thing most likely to close this file is a change nobody has to go
// looking for. It survives on the size of a measured population, not on nobody having tried.
//
// PRE-EXISTING, MEASURED RATHER THAN INHERITED: graded `check-clean invalid wasm` on the
// merge base of the commit that pinned it (seed 1,463,730) and on its shipped seed
// (1,464,519), the same sentence at the same offset both times, and its module is
// BYTE-IDENTICAL across the change (3,392 bytes, `cmp`-equal).
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty.
type Circle = { r: i32 | null }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Box1 = {[string]: Circle}
type Box2 = {[string]: Circle}
type GW = { g: {[string]: Circle} }
function useShape(s: Shape): i32 { if s is Sq { return 1 } return 0 }
const sqv: Sq = { s: 1 }
const _sp1: Box1 = Map()
const _sp2: Box2 = Map()
function mkcall() {
  const cc = Map()
  cc["k0"] = { r: null }
  return cc
}
function outer() {
  const lam = () => {
    const wv: GW = { g: mkcall() }
    if useShape(sqv) > 99 { print(0) }
    const g0 = (wv.g)["k0"] ?? { r: null }
    if (g0).r != null { print(7) } else { print(0) }
  }
  lam()
}
outer()
